  "walkthrough": [
    "`user-message` is published on `main` from outside the network; `router` picks it up, and `auditLog`, which has no `listensTo` and so takes every event on `main`, gets a copy too.",
    "`router` receives it and emits `task` on `work`, a channel that only carries `task`; `worker` takes it from there, and `auditLog` gets a copy too because it also subscribes to `work`.",
    "`worker` receives it and emits `answer` on `client`, a channel that only carries `answer`; no agent subscribes to `client`, so `answer` leaves the network through its `sse` proxy and, as a terminal event, ends the run.",
    "The runtime then publishes `m4trix:run.completed` on every channel (`main`, `work` and `client`) to close the run; runtime events never invoke agents, so not even `auditLog` receives it."
  ]
